{"__lines":{"North of the peaks, a wood of white birches stands around a black lake, and half of it has gone black with thorn. Red fruit hangs from the black half. Nothing eats it.":"st_palewood_0","A witch in a wide black hat is waiting for you on a stump, eating one of the red fruits. \u201cRelax. I am the thief, not the monster. The monster is the one who sent you here.\u201d":"st_palewood_1","Jessamy Crow, the Hex-Thief, steals the Pilfered Hexes back from a church that stole them first. She will not give you the way to the Gate for free. Nobody here gives anything for free.":"st_palewood_2","Jessamy was right about one thing: something is eating the Tithe faster than anyone can pay it. The trail leads back down, under Cindermarch, to a throne made of coins and bones.":"st_throne2_0","Jessamy is beside you, for once not stealing anything. Ilsabet checks her knives twice. \u201cNo one opens a door she is standing in. So we move her.\u201d":"st_atonement_2","He will fight beside you once, in your next duel, with his Blaze Titan.":"st_envoy_burn2"},"st_palewood_0":"img/x/3db05e2f6b3c7935.mp3","st_palewood_1":"img/x/d99a263adfc71da2.mp3","st_palewood_2":"img/x/0e32e429521660fb.mp3","st_throne2_0":"img/x/6e34b7915aaa7d92.mp3","st_atonement_2":"img/x/ae6046845785cc0b.mp3","st_envoy_burn2":"img/x/85ec185c28d2b14f.mp3"}